## Two things beyond the literal ask, both flagged
I patched the **generators**, because the old text lived in `be_wtc_data_part1/part7.py`, `build_be_wtc.py` and `_build_payslip.py` — a rebuild would have silently reverted both fixes, the failure mode the tax-engine pass established a rule against. The WTC splices were done by tokenising the source and substituting literals built from the corrected workbook cells, so nothing was retyped; all four reconstruct byte-for-byte.

